# THE BUILD CONTEXT IS THIS WHOLE REPOSITORY, and it is uploaded to the docker
# daemon or to a remote builder BEFORE any instruction runs. `deploy/compose/
# docker-compose.yaml` builds with `context: ../..` because the Dockerfile
# installs this package from source, so a FILLED-IN `deploy/compose/.env` —
# which is git-ignored and therefore invisible to every other guard here —
# travelled with every `docker compose … --build`, carrying its DSN and its
# password to whatever daemon ran the build, even though the Dockerfile never
# copies it into the image (Copilot review of openDox-code#25, round 19).
# `.gitignore` is not a build-context rule; this file is the one docker reads.
#
# AN ALLOWLIST, NOT A DENYLIST, so the property is structural rather than a
# list somebody has to remember to extend: everything is excluded and the four
# paths `deploy/compose/Dockerfile` actually COPYs are named back in. A secret
# that arrives in a file nobody anticipated is excluded by the first line
# rather than by an entry nobody wrote, and adding a COPY without adding its
# source here fails the build loudly instead of shipping quietly.
# `tests_runtime/test_deploy_shape.py` derives the list below from the
# Dockerfile's own COPY lines, so the two cannot drift.
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!src
!migrations
